A well-formed directive on an empty declaration group attaches to nothing: no spec
exists to become a provider, and the group doc is consumed by the group scan, so without
a dedicated check the directive would be silently inert, the one thing a directive must
never be. Rejected as misplaced, located at the directive.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrMisplacedDirective
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

type Config struct{}

//plumb:build
var ()

//plumb:build
func NewConfig() *Config { return &Config{} }
